## 2. Decoupled Architecture Pattern (Implemented)

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as Client Browser
    participant Vercel as Next.js Vercel Edge (/api/synthetic/generate)
    participant Express as Express Backend API (/api/synthetic/generate)
    participant Engine as SyntheticPipeline Engine
    participant Storage as MongoDB / File Store

    User->>Vercel: POST /api/synthetic/generate (count: 25, seed: 42)
    Note over Vercel: Lightweight REST Proxy (<5 KB Bundle)
    Vercel->>Express: POST ${BACKEND_API_URL}/api/synthetic/generate
    Note over Express: Standalone Node Service (Railway)
    Express->>Engine: pipeline.generateDataset(config)
    Engine->>Storage: Write synthetic documents & ground-truth JSONs
    Engine-->>Express: Return GenerationReport
    Express-->>Vercel: 200 OK (JSON Payload)
    Vercel-->>User: 200 OK (JSON Response)
```

---

## 3. Advantages of the Decoupled Proxy Architecture

1. **Zero Serverless Size Penalties**: Vercel serverless function sizes remain **< 5 KB**, well below the 250 MB limit (and below our target of 100 MB).
2. **Instant Deployments**: Vercel build times reduced from **51 seconds** to **23 seconds**.
3. **No Large Functions Required**: Operates natively within standard Vercel Hobby & Pro tiers without relying on beta flags or paid add-ons.
4. **Complete Preservation of Research Functionality**: All synthetic generator templates, quality profiles, normalizer rules, and error taxonomies remain 100% intact on the Express backend.

